  "configuration_id": "config_005",
  "reason": "Existing evidence shows multiprofile avgpool RNA with PCA is strong (0.591), multimodal concat with resnet50 improves it to 0.619, and replacing PCA with scVI in that multimodal setting gives a small accuracy gain (0.632) but slightly lower F1, so the value of scVI is not yet isolated. config_005 tests scVI in the same RNA-only multiprofile avgpool setting as config_002, changing only the RNA encoder. This clarifies whether the RNA representation itself improves over PCA or whether the multimodal scVI gain is due to interaction or noise, and it also indicates how much image fusion is contributing. Under limited budget, this single-factor RNA-only experiment reduces uncertainty about a key representation decision before committing further to scVI multimodal variants."
}

